-- title:
--   Theorem 5.4, pp. 15–16 — resolvent, hitting and exit identities for a Markov branching process with immigration
-- statement:
--   Let $(X,\mathbb P)$ be an MBI with parameters $(\alpha,\mu,p,\beta,\nu,q)$ on $E=\{0,1,2,\dots\}$, with mechanisms $\psi,\phi$, root $s_0$, and the sequences $W,\pi,\varpi$ of Lemma 5.1 ($W(z)=0$ for $z\le-1$). For $x,y\ge0$ let
--   $$\mathscr H^{[y}(x)=\sum_{l=0}^{y-x-1}\pi(y-x-1-l)\,\frac{(W\star\varpi)(l)}{l+x+1}\qquad(=0\text{ if }y\le x),$$
--   and $I(x)=\int_0^{s_0}\frac{v^x}{\psi(v)}\exp\big(-\int_0^v\frac{\phi(u)}{\psi(u)}du\big)dv$. Then for $x\ge0$ and $s\in[0,s_0)$,
--   $$\sum_{y\ge0}\mathscr H^{[y}(x)s^y=\int_0^s\frac{v^x}{\psi(v)}\exp\Big(\int_v^s\frac{\phi(u)}{\psi(u)}du\Big)dv,$$
--   and if $\beta=q=0$ then $\mathscr H^{[y}(x)=W(y-x-1)/y$. Moreover:
--
--   1. If all states are transient, then $I(x)<\infty$ and $G(x,y)=\pi(y)I(x)-\mathscr H^{[y}(x)$ for $x,y\ge0$. If the MBI is an MBP, then for $x\ge0$, $y\ge1$,
--   $$G(x,y)=\tfrac1y\big(s_0^xW(y-1)-W(y-x-1)\big).$$
--   2. If all states are transient, then for $x,y\ge0$
--   $$\mathbb P_x(T_y<\zeta)=\frac{\pi(y)I(x)-\mathscr H^{[y}(x)}{\pi(y)I(y)};$$
--   if the MBI is an MBP, then $\mathbb P_x(T_y<\zeta)=\frac{s_0^xW(y-1)-W(y-x-1)}{s_0^yW(y-1)}$ for $y\ge1$ and $=s_0^x$ for $y=0$; if all states are recurrent, $\mathbb P_x(T_y<\zeta)=1$.
--   3. In any case, for $0\le a\le x\le b-1$,
--   $$\mathbb P_x(T_a<T_{[b}\wedge\zeta)=\frac{\mathscr H^{[b}(x)}{\mathscr H^{[b}(a)},\qquad \mathbb P_x(T_{(a,b)^\complement}<\zeta)=1-\sum_{z=a+1}^{b-1}(pz+q)\Big(\frac{\mathscr H^{[b}(x)}{\mathscr H^{[b}(a)}\mathscr H^{[z}(a)-\mathscr H^{[z}(x)\Big),$$
--   $$\mathbb P_x(T_{[b}<\zeta)=\begin{cases}1-\sum_{z=0}^{b-1}(pz+q)\Big(\frac{\pi(z)}{\pi(b)}\mathscr H^{[b}(x)-\mathscr H^{[z}(x)\Big), & \beta+q>0,\\[6pt] 1+p\sum_{z=0}^{b-x-2}W(z)-\frac{W(b-x-1)}{W(b-1)}\Big(1+p\sum_{z=0}^{b-2}W(z)\Big), & \beta=q=0.\end{cases}$$
--
--   This is the full set of fluctuation identities for MBIs: resolvent, point-hitting probabilities, two-sided exit and upward first passage, in each of the three regimes (all transient, all recurrent, MBP).
--
--   **Formalization Note** The MBI is the chain generated by `mbiQ P` on `Set.Ici (0 : ℤ)`. No division by zero is reachable in item (3): $\mathscr H^{[b}(a)>0$ and $W(b-1)>0$ for $a<b$, and $\pi(b)>0$ when $\beta+q>0$. No positivity hypothesis is added.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: parameter constraints of p. 12 (α > 0, µ, ν probability measures, µ(0) > 0, µ(1) = 0, p, β, q ≥ 0) → MBIParams.Valid, with HasSum µ 1, HasSum ν 1 and ν(0) = 0; reason: same constraints
--   - encoding: E = ℤ ∩ [0, ∞), states x, y ≥ 0 → Set.Ici (0 : ℤ), with natural-number arguments cast to ℤ; reason: same states
--   - encoding: the Markov chain (X, ℙ) generated by Q (jump chain/holding time definition, p. 2) → transition, resolvent, hitProb, hitBeforeProb, exitDist, killedResolvent computed from jump-chain path sums with Exp(1) holding clocks; reason: this is the paper's construction (i)–(iv); the cemetery ∂ is represented by leaving E
--   - encoding: real-valued probabilities ℙ_x(…) → ℝ≥0∞-valued path sums compared through .toReal; reason: a probability is at most 1, so .toReal loses nothing
--   - encoding: all states in E are transient → AllTransient E Q: G(x, x) < ∞ for every x ∈ E; reason: Norris, Markov Chains, Theorem 3.4.2, which the paper itself invokes on p. 3; an absorbing state has G(x, x) = ∞
--   - encoding: all states recurrent → AllRecurrent: G(x, x) = ∞ for every x ≥ 0; reason: Norris, Theorem 3.4.2, as for transience
--   - encoding: MBP, i.e. β = q = 0 → IsMBP P := P.beta = 0 ∧ P.q = 0; reason: the paper's definition, p. 12
--   - encoding: I(x) = ∫_0^{s₀} … dv as a real number in (1) and (2) → IntI P x, an ℝ≥0∞ lintegral, with conclusion clause IntI P x ≠ ⊤ under transience, then .toReal; reason: the integral diverges in the recurrent case, where a Bochner integral would be 0; the clause is what the paper's real formula presupposes
--   - encoding: G(x, y) as a real number in (1) → conclusion clause resolvent … ≠ ⊤, then .toReal; reason: G is ℝ≥0∞-valued; finite by transience (p. 3) and, for the MBP with y ≥ 1, by the formula
--   - encoding: W(z) = 0 for z ≤ −1 → Wz P z on ℤ; W P on ℕ where the argument is a true natural number (y − 1 with y ≥ 1, b − x − 1 with b ≥ x + 1); reason: avoids truncated natural subtraction
--   - encoding: Σ_{z=a+1}^{b−1}, Σ_{z=0}^{b−1}, Σ_{z=0}^{b−x−2}, Σ_{z=0}^{b−2} → Finset.Ioo a b, range b, range (b − x − 1), range (b − 1); reason: the same index sets for b ≥ x + 1 ≥ 1; empty sums where the paper's are empty
--   - encoding: case 'β = q = 0' of the last identity → else branch of 'if 0 < β + q'; reason: β, q ≥ 0, so ¬(0 < β + q) ↔ β = q = 0
--   - encoding: ℋ^{[y}(x) = W(y−x−1)/y for x, y ≥ 0 (at y = 0 the right side is the undefined 0/0, the left side the empty sum 0) → calH P y x = Wz P (y − x − 1) / y for all x y : ℕ, where Lean's 0/0 = 0; reason: only the undefined case y = 0 is affected, and there both sides are 0
-- source:
--   Loeffen, Patie, Wang, Fluctuation Theory of Continuous-Time, Skip-Free Downward Markov Chains with Applications to Branching Processes with Immigration, arXiv:2208.14425v1, pp. 15–16, Theorem 5.4

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Chain
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Model
open scoped ENNReal Topology
open Filter MeasureTheory

namespace SkipFreeFluct.MBI

/-- Theorem 5.4, pp. 15–16: the fluctuation identities of an MBI with parameters
`(α, µ, p, β, ν, q)`, state space `E = ℤ ∩ [0, ∞)` and Q-matrix (5.1).
* The generating function of `y ↦ ℋ^{[y}(x)` on `[0, s₀)`, and its MBP form `W(y - x - 1)/y`.
* (1) The resolvent if all states are transient, and if the MBI is an MBP (`y ≥ 1`).
* (2) `ℙ_x(T_y < ζ)` if all states are transient, if it is an MBP, and if all states are
  recurrent.
* (3) In any case, for `0 ≤ a ≤ x ≤ b - 1`: the one-sided-before-two-sided hitting probability,
  the probability of leaving `(a, b)` and the probability of reaching `[b, ∞)`. -/
theorem theorem_5_4 (P : MBIParams) (hP : P.Valid) :
    (∀ x : ℕ, ∀ s ∈ Set.Ico 0 (s0 P),
      HasSum (fun y : ℕ => calH P y x * s ^ y)
        (∫ v in (0 : ℝ)..s,
          v ^ x / psi P v * Real.exp (∫ u in v..s, phiImm P u / psi P u))) ∧
    (IsMBP P → ∀ x y : ℕ, calH P y x = Wz P ((y : ℤ) - x - 1) / y) ∧
    (AllTransient (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) → ∀ x y : ℕ,
      IntI P x ≠ ⊤ ∧ resolvent (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) x y ≠ ⊤ ∧
      (resolvent (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) x y).toReal = piSeq P y * (IntI P x).toReal - calH P y x) ∧
    (IsMBP P → ∀ x y : ℕ, 1 ≤ y →
      resolvent (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) x y ≠ ⊤ ∧
      (resolvent (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) x y).toReal =
        1 / y * (s0 P ^ x * W P (y - 1) - Wz P ((y : ℤ) - x - 1))) ∧
    (AllTransient (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) → ∀ x y : ℕ,
      (hitProb (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) {(y : ℤ)} x).toReal =
        (piSeq P y * (IntI P x).toReal - calH P y x) / (piSeq P y * (IntI P y).toReal)) ∧
    (IsMBP P → ∀ x y : ℕ,
      (hitProb (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) {(y : ℤ)} x).toReal =
        if 1 ≤ y then
          (s0 P ^ x * W P (y - 1) - Wz P ((y : ℤ) - x - 1)) / (s0 P ^ y * W P (y - 1))
        else s0 P ^ x) ∧
    (AllRecurrent (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) → ∀ x y : ℕ,
      hitProb (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) {(y : ℤ)} x = 1) ∧
    (∀ a x b : ℕ, a ≤ x → x + 1 ≤ b →
      (hitBeforeProb (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) {(a : ℤ)} (Set.Ici (b : ℤ)) x).toReal =
          calH P b x / calH P b a ∧
      (hitProb (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) (Set.Ioo (a : ℤ) b)ᶜ x).toReal =
          1 - ∑ z ∈ Finset.Ioo a b,
            (P.p * z + P.q) * (calH P b x / calH P b a * calH P z a - calH P z x) ∧
      (hitProb (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P) (Set.Ici (b : ℤ)) x).toReal =
          if 0 < P.beta + P.q then
            1 - ∑ z ∈ Finset.range b,
              (P.p * z + P.q) * (piSeq P z / piSeq P b * calH P b x - calH P z x)
          else
            1 + P.p * (∑ z ∈ Finset.range (b - x - 1), W P z) -
              W P (b - x - 1) / W P (b - 1) * (1 + P.p * ∑ z ∈ Finset.range (b - 1), W P z)) := by sorry

end SkipFreeFluct.MBI
